  "feedbacks": [],
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 29 actions (src/actions.js, each assigned as actions.<id> = {...} in initActions). The module registers no feedbacks: src/feedbacks.js builds an empty object and calls setFeedbackDefinitions with it (src/feedbacks.js:6-11). Variables (src/variables.js) and presets (src/presets.js) are not catalogued.",
    "Protocol: HTTP POST to http(s)://<host>:<port>/api/0<command> with an \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" header, sent to the primary PVP and to the optional backup PVP (src/api.js:51-94, config fields host, port, https, auth and the *_backup variants in src/config.js). Ports are only accepted when above 1024 and up to 65535 (src/api.js:11-13). Not run against PVP.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.1: options do not support expressions. No option sets useVariables, but every textinput option is passed through parseVariablesInString in its callback, so $(...) variables work in practice (except where noted); they are recorded here exactly as the source declares them.",
    "IDs (Layer ID, Playlist ID, Cue ID) are free text: a name, a UUID or a numeric index. checkId throws when a numeric index is below the minimum: Layer and Cue 0, Playlist -1 (-1 means \"Video Input\"; src/api.js:100-157). Defaults are the source value \"0\" and are kept.",
    "Possible defects seen when reading, not run: in the relative branch of opacity (actions.js:318-319) and in goToLayerOffset (551, 555) and skipLayerSeconds (583) the callbacks use a variable `opt` that is not declared in those callbacks; layerEffectPreset uses `pt.idx` (279) which is not declared either. workspaceTransitionDuration calls parseVariablesInString on action.options.idx, which that action has no option for (632). These would raise errors at runtime if the code path is reached; this was not checked against a running module.",
    "opacity: the second option declares regex: self.REGEX_SIGNED_NUMBER (actions.js:298). That name is defined nowhere in the module repository nor in @companion-module/base 1.15.0 (checked in a local copy; the 1.4.x dist itself was not inspected), so no regex is recorded. A leading + or - makes the value relative (read current opacity, then add), otherwise it is absolute; values are clamped to 0-100 and sent as a fraction (src/api.js:158-162).",
    "Duration options (layerTransitionDuration, workspaceTransitionDuration) are clamped to 0-5 seconds by the module (actions.js:614, 637). goToLayerOffset: a leading \"-\" means seconds from the end, otherwise from the start. skipLayerSeconds: the sign gives the direction. A comment says the /layerBlend/ endpoint used by trackMatte works but is not documented by the vendor (actions.js:366-367)."
  ]
}
